   "evidence": "Docstring of `def ReadsFrom`: 'The readings of `C'` are read off from those of `C`'; the third conjunct is `C'.coord i' s y = L i i' y (C.coord i s (\u03c4 i i' y))`, so C' is computed from C while C is the receiver of the dot notation.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Sobolev/Atlas/ChartData.lean",
   "fix": "Either swap the arguments so that `C'.ReadsFrom C \u03bc` means C' is read off from C, or keep the order and rename to a source-first verb (e.g. `C.Determines C' \u03bc` / `ReadsInto`). Update all listed declarations together.",
   "issue": "`C.ReadsFrom C' \u03bc` is documented as 'the readings of C' are read off from those of C', but with dot notation it reads as 'C reads from C''. That inverts the direction and clashes with the source-first `TransfersTo C C'`, e.g. `changeAtlas_injective` takes `hC' : C'.ReadsFrom C \u03bc` to mean C is read off from C'. The same inversion affects `readsFrom_iff`, `ReadsFrom.intro`, `readsFrom_refl`, `ReadsFrom.coord_ae_eq`, the hC/hC' arguments of `changeAtlas`/`atlasEquiv`/`changeAtlas_injective`/`exists_norm_changeAtlas_le`, `FiniteBundleAtlas.readsFrom_sectionChartData` (Sobolev/Atlas/Equiv.lean) and `FiniteBundleAtlas.readsFrom_halfSectionChartData` (Bordered/Atlas/Equiv.lean).",
